% Regression: caching an execform builds a raster device and fetched the
% rectangle-fill C operators (.fillrectrgb / .fillrectgray) by name with load.
% Once those operators were relocated out of systemdict into .internaldict, the
% load failed with undefined and every cached form broke. They are now fetched
% through //.internaldict /X get.
%
% Run through the ppm device by run-ps-test.sh, and it has to be a device that
% keeps its page as rows: the cache is only built where the device holds such a
% page, so a run on a device that paints nothing takes the uncached path and
% reaches none of what this exists to guard. Prints SUCCESS iff a cacheable form
% runs through execform without error.

/faildict 1 dict def faildict /n 0 put
/assert { % bool (name) . -
    exch { pop }{ (FAIL: )print print (\n)print faildict /n 2 copy get 1 add put } ifelse
} bind def

/F <<
    /FormType 1
    /BBox [0 0 120 120]
    /Matrix [1 0 0 1 0 0]
    /PaintProc {
        pop
        0 0 120 120 rectfill
        1 setgray 20 20 80 80 rectfill
    }
>> def

% execform the same form twice: the first pass populates the form cache (the
% path that builds the raster device and clears it with the rect-fill
% operators), the second pass replays from the cache. Neither may error.
{ gsave F execform grestore
  gsave F execform grestore } stopped not
    (a cacheable form runs through execform without error) assert

faildict /n get 0 eq { (SUCCESS\n) print } { faildict /n get =print ( failures\n) print } ifelse
flush
quit
